    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Fundamental Duties were NOT part of the original 1950 Constitution; they were added in 1976 during the Emergency.",
        "Fundamental Rights apply to both citizens and foreigners, but Fundamental Duties apply strictly ONLY to Indian citizens.",
        "The 11th Fundamental Duty [Article 51A(k)], concerning education for children aged 6 to 14, was added by the 86th Amendment Act, 2002."
      ],
      "id": "5pa59g0"
